{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he took curd, etc.</b> And he did not bring bread, because Sarah's menstruation had resumed — that day the way of women returned to her, and the dough became impure (Bava Metzia ibid.)." "<b>Curd.</b> The fat of milk that is gathered from its surface." "<b>And the calf that he made.</b> That he prepared; one by one as he prepared each, I would bring and set it before them." "<b>And they ate.</b> They appeared as though they ate — from here, a person should not deviate from the custom (Bava Metzia ibid.)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:11.728263165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}